+## Acceptance Suite Defect Analysis (2026-07-28)
+
+The external browser acceptance suite (Cypress) reports 5 failures. These are PRODUCT defects, not test issues.
+
+### Defect 1: DOM node replacement during state changes (4 failures)
+
+**Acceptance failures:**
+- "Mark all as completed" → should allow me to mark all items as completed
+- "Mark all as completed" → should allow me to clear the complete state of all items
+- "Item" → should allow me to mark items as complete
+- "Item" → should allow me to un-mark items as complete
+
+**Root cause:** The `render()` function in `app.js` calls `todoList.innerHTML = ''` which destroys ALL DOM nodes and recreates them from scratch. This causes Cypress to lose its element references.
+
+**Verification suite coverage:** `dom-stability.feature` (5 scenarios) already captures this defect and fails correctly.
+
+**Required fix:** Mutate existing DOM nodes in place (toggle class/checkbox) instead of rebuilding the list.
+
+### Defect 2: Toggle checkbox visible during editing (1 failure)
+
+**Acceptance failure:**
+- "Editing" → should hide other controls when editing
+
+**Root cause:** The CSS packages (`todomvc-app-css`, `todomvc-common`) are not installed, so the rule `li.editing .view { display: none }` is not applied.
+
+**Verification suite coverage:** `editing-controls.feature` now has 7 scenarios:
+- Behavioral check: "The toggle checkbox is not visible during editing" (newly added, fails)
+- Source checks: CSS packages declared, files exist, rule present (all fail)
+
+**Required fix:** Install CSS packages and ensure stylesheets are linked.
+
